--TEST--
`Core\Request\Part::saveTo`'s path is a sink and `filename()` is the client's claim, so the one line every upload traversal has been written on does not compile — `rule:http-server/a-part-is-a-file-iff-it-carries-a-filename` and `rule:core-classes/io-write-stream`, `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:core-classes/io-write-stream` makes `saveTo` a delegation to `Core\IO::writeStream`, and this
// is the whole of what that buys: `writeStream`'s path is already an `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`
// path sink, with no exemption for a name that arrived by way of an upload, so
// a destination the part chose for itself is refused at the call rather than
// checked somewhere inside it.
//
// What is refused here is `move_uploaded_file($tmp, $dir . $_FILES['x']['name'])`
// -- one line, reading as obviously correct, and the traversal. `filename()` is
// `tainted string` because a peer wrote it, the parameter is `string`, and
// `Core\IO::within` is the only way across.
foreach (Core\Request::files() as Core\Request\Part $part) {
    $part->saveTo($part->filename());
}
// covers: Core\Request\Part::saveTo
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
   --> case.nvs:13:19
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
